hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1352","Umm Habibah, daughter of Jahsh, sister-in-law of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and wife of 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, had a flow of blood for seven years. She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is not menstruation but only vein; so you should take a bath and pray. 'Aishah said: She used to take bath in a wash-tub in the apartment of her sister Zainab daughter of Jahsh ; the redness of (her) blood dominated the water. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 288)"
"1353","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Auf (may Allah be pleased with him). Her sister, Lady Zainab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her), who was the honorable wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), this woman suffered from istihada for seven years. She complained about this to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is not menstruation, it is the discharge of another vein. You should perform ghusl and continue to offer prayers. So that woman used to perform ghusl for every prayer. She would sit in her sister's tub, and the redness of the blood would dominate the water."
"1354","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: This is not menstruation, rather it is blood from some other vein. When menstruation comes, then during those specific days in which you used to have your period before, leave the prayer, and when those days pass, then perform ghusl and do wudu for every prayer."
"1355","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was asked about a woman suffering from istihada (non-menstrual bleeding), so he said: She should leave the prayer during her specific days, then perform ghusl once, and then perform wudu for every prayer."
"1356","I said: She is in the state of menstruation. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Her menstruation is not in her hand."
"1357","The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) said to me; Get me the mat from the mosque. I said ; I am menstruating. The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) then replied: Your menstruation is not in your hand. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 261)"
"1358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your menstruation is not in your hand."" So I handed him the (mat). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration has been reported by A'mash from Thabit bin Ubaid, and also from Qasim, both from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1359","""I used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was menstruating."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 277)"
"1360","I was in a state of menstruation. I would drink water from it, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would take that vessel and place his blessed mouth at the spot where I had placed my mouth and drink the water. Similarly, when I would suck on a bone while in a state of menstruation, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would take it and place his mouth at the same spot where I had placed my mouth."
"1361","I would bring a vessel to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). I would drink from it, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) would take it and place his mouth at the spot where I had placed my mouth and drink from it. Similarly, I would take a bone with meat on it and eat from it, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) would place his mouth at the spot where I had placed my mouth and eat from it, even though I would be in a state of menstruation at that time."
"1362","Among the jews, when a women menstruated, they ejected her from the house, and they did not eat with her, nor did they drink with her, nor did they associate with her in (their houses) so the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) was questioned about that. Thereupon Allah revealed : “They question thee concerning menstruation. Say : I: is an illness, so let woman alone at such times” (ii 222). The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) then said: Associate with them in the houses and do everything except sexual intercourse. Thereupon the Jews said: This man does not want to leave anything we do without opposing us in it. Usaid b. Hudair and Abbad b. Bishr came and said: Messenger of Allah, the jews are saying such and such a thing. Shall we not then have intercourse with women during mensuration? The face of the Apostle Allah ﷺ underwent such a change that we thought he was angry with them; but when they went out they received a gift of milk which was being brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he sent after them and gave them a drink, whereupon we thought that he was not angry with them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 258)"
"1363","""While I was lying down with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a blanket, my period came, so I slipped away and put on the clothes I used to wear when I was menstruating. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Are you menstruating?' I said: 'Yes.' Then he called me and I lied down with him under the blanket."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 283)"
"1364","embraced her. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 268)"
"1365","The Prophet ﷺ would contact and embrace any of his wives while she was menstruating. She would wear the wrapper up to half the the thighs or cover her knees with it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 267)"
"1366","I would be in the state of menstruation."
"1367","embraced her. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 268)"
"1368","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would lie with any of his noble wives and she was in a state of menstruation at that time, he would instruct her to tie a waist-wrapper."
"1369","""And he came close to me and reached out his hand. I said: 'I am Junub.' He said: 'The Muslim is not made impure (Najis).'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 268)"
"1370","""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met a man from among his Companions, he would shake hands with him and supplicate for him. I saw him one day in the early morning, and I tried to avoid him, then I came to him later in the day. He said: 'I saw you but you were avoiding me.' I said: 'I was Junub and I was afraid that you would touch me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The Muslim is not made impure (Najis).'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 267)"
"1371","The person who shaved heads was sitting beside him. On that day, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) straightened his hair with his blessed hand, then he took the hair from the right side of his head in his fist and said to the barber: ""Shave it."" So he shaved it. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) distributed those hairs among the people present with him that day, giving one or two to each. Then he took the hair from the left side of his head in his fist and said to the barber: ""Shave it."" So he shaved it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) called Sayyiduna Abu Talhah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) and gave those hairs to him. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) distributing his hair among his companions is a clear statement that a person's hair is pure, because the noble companions acquired the blessed hair of the Prophet (peace be upon him) in order to seek blessings through it. So some kept it in their waistbands, some held it in their hands, some kept it in their collars, and they would perform prayers with them and fulfill their needs while the blessed hair was with them. To the extent that most of them made a will that the blessed hair be placed in their shrouds. If this hair were impure, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would not have distributed an impure thing among the people, especially when he knew that they would seek blessings in the manner we have mentioned. So when this matter is authentically established regarding the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), it is also authentically established regarding his Ummah, because it is impossible that something is pure from the existence of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the same thing is impure from his Ummah."
"1372","The Prophet sprinkled water over it and did not wash that spot."",""The Prophet ﷺ  used to bring young boys and pat their cheeks. One time"",""a young boy urinated on him"","" so he followed him with water and did not wash him."""""""""
"1373","""I came to the Messenger of Allah with a son of mine who was not yet eating solid food, and he (the baby) urinated on him. He called for water and sprinkled it over (the urine)."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 524)"
"1374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took him and seated him in his lap. The child urinated on the clothes of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took water and sprinkled it on that spot. He did not wash it. Ibn Shihab says: After this, it became customary that the urine of a child is not washed until he is able to eat something. When he starts eating, then his urine is to be washed."
"1375","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding the urine of a nursing infant: Water should be sprinkled over the urine of a boy, and the urine of a girl should be washed."
"1376","I still seem to see the glistening of the perfume where the hair was parted on the head of the Messenger of Allah (SWAS) while he was wearing Ihram. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1746)"
"1377","I still seem to see the glistening of the perfume where the hair was parted on the head of the Messenger of Allah (SWAS) while he was wearing Ihram. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1746)"
"1378","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Musk is the purest of all fragrances."
"1379","A person stayed in the house of A'isha and in the morning began to wash his garment. A'isha said: In case you saw it (i. e. drop of semen), it would have served the purpose (of purifying the garment) if you had simply washed that spot; and in case you did not see it, it would have been enough to sprinkle water around it, for when I saw that on the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I simply scraped it off and he offered prayer, while putting that on. (Using translation from Muslim 288a)"
"1380","""I remember rubbing the Janabah from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 300)"
"1381","I used to wash the traces of Janaba (semen) from the clothes of the Prophet ﷺ and he used to go for prayers while traces of water were still on it (water spots were still visible). (Using translation from Bukhārī 229)"
"1382","I used to wash semen (i.e., janabah) from the clothes of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and he would go for prayer while the mark of water would still be visible on his clothes. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to wash semen from the clothes of the Prophet (peace be upon him) when it was wet, because in this case a person feels more cleanliness, and when it was dry, Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to scrape it off, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) would perform prayer in those clothes. We also give fatwa according to this, and we adopt this opinion that when semen is wet, it should be washed for the satisfaction of the mind, not because it is impure, and when semen is dry, it is sufficient to scrape it off in accordance with the Sunnah."
"1383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Do you want this? He replied: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised both his hands. His hands had not yet come down when a cloud gave shade and it started to rain. The people filled everything they had with water. After that, we observed that nowhere ahead of the army had it rained (meaning, the rain had only fallen over the army). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The people squeezing the water from the camel’s dung and placing it on their liver, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) not commanding them to wash off what was on their bodies, is evidence that the dung of animals whose meat is eaten is pure."
"1384","The Messenger of Allah said: ""If you cannot find anywhere (for prayer) except sheep's resting-places and camels' resting-places, then perform prayer in the sheep's resting-places and do not perform prayer in the camels' resting-places."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 768)"
"1385","Anas said, ""The Prophet ﷺ prayed in the sheep fold."" Later on I heard him saying, ""He prayed in the sheep folds before the construction of the, mosque."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 429)"
"1386","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Some Bedouins from the tribe of ‘Uraina came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The climate of Madinah did not suit them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to drink the milk and urine of camels. They drank it and became healthy. Then they killed the shepherd of the camels and drove the camels away. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent peo"
"1387","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered the people belonging to the tribe of ‘Uraina to drink the milk and urine of cam"
"1388","The climate of Madinah did not suit them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent them to his camels. He instructed, ""Drink their milk and their urine."" They drank it and became healthy and robust. Then they killed the shepherd of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and drove away the camels. Those people had become apostates. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent people after them. They were captured and brought back. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered their hands and feet to be cut off, their eyes to be branded with heated irons, and they were thrown onto burning stones."
"1389","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not drink it."" I submitted, ""Can we use it as medicine for our sick?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is a disease, not a cure."
"1390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is not a medicine, rather it is a disease."
"1391","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came, and it had started to ferment. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What is this? Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: One of my daughters is ill, so we have prepared nabidh for her. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted has not placed your cure in that which is forbidden."
"1392","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was asked about a mouse that dies in clarified butter (ghee). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: If the ghee was solid, then throw away the mouse and the ghee around it, and eat the remaining ghee. But if the ghee was melted, then do not use it."
"1393","the Prophet was asked about a mouse that fell into the cooking fat. He said: ""If it (the fat) is solid, then throw it away, and whatever is around it. If it is liquid then do not use it at all.""(Daif) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4260)"
"1394","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about a mouse that falls into clarified butter (ghee) and dies. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If the ghee is solid, throw away that mouse and the ghee around it, and eat the remaining ghee. But if it is liquid, then do not go near it. Imam Abdur Razzaq narrates that Abdur Rahman bin Buzwayh informed me that the narrator named Ma'mar also mentioned that this narration is transmitted from Zuhri, from Ubaydullah bin Abdullah, from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from Sayyidah Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a similar manner."
"1395","""I asked the Messenger of Allah about menstrual blood that gets on clothing. He said, 'Wash it with water and lote leaves, and rub it, even with a piece of stick.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 628)"
"1396","The command to scrape and sprinkle water is for recommendation, not obligation, and the command to rub it with water is connected to its condition, which is the removal of the impurity. So, the removal of the impurity is obligatory, and rubbing it with water is supererogatory, if it is possible to remove the impurity without rubbing. And after washing the garment, the command to pray in that garment is for permissibility, not for obligation."
"1397","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was asked about a garment on which menstrual blood gets stained. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: The woman should wash it with water, then sprinkle water over it, and then she may pray in that (garment)."
"1398","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Scrape it off, wash it with water, and sprinkle water on the surrounding area."
"1399","""A Bedouin stood up and urinated in the Masjid, ans the people started shouting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'Leave him alone, and spill a bucket of water over his urine. For you have been sent to make things easy for people, you have not been sent to make things difficult.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 56)"
"1400","A bedouin urinated in the mosque, and the people rushed to beat him. Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to leave him and pour a bucket or a tumbler (full) of water over the place where he has passed urine. The Prophet then said, "" You have been sent to make things easy (for the people) and you have not been sent to make things difficult for them."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6128)"
"1401","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sitting in the mosque. During this time, a Bedouin came in and began to urinate while sitting. The companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Stop, stop! The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Do not try to stop him while he is urinating. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) called that person and said: It is not appropriate to bring impurity or relieve oneself inside these mosques, or whatever else the Prophet (peace be upon him) said. The Qur'an is recited here, or Allah is remembered here. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) called for a bucket of water and poured it over the spot."
"1402","""A Bedouin entered the mosque when the Messenger of Allah was sitting there, and (the man) said: 'O Allah, forgive me and Muhammed, and do not forgive anyone else with us.' The Messenger of Allah smiled and said: 'You have placed restrictions on something that is vast.' Then the Bedouin turned away, went to a corner of the mosque, spread his legs and began to urinate. After he had a better understanding, the Bedouin said: 'He got up and came to me, and may my father and mother be ransomed for him, he did not rebuke me nor revile me. He said: ""This mosque is not for urinating in. Rather it is built for the remembrance of Allah and prayer.'"" Then he called for a large vessel of water and poured it over the place where he had urinated."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 529)"
"1403","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When any one of you treads with his sandal upon an unclean place, the earth will render it purified. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 385)"
"1404","When any of you treads with his shoes upon something unclean, they will be purified with the earth. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 386)"
"1405","I brought a bowl or a vessel of water to him. He performed istinja (cleaning) with it, then he wiped his left hand on the ground and washed it. Then I brought (more) water in the vessel to him, and he performed wudu (ablution)."
"1406","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: These privies are frequented by the jinns and devils. So when anyone amongst you goes there, he should say: ""I seek refuge in Allah from male and female devils."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 6)"
"1407","""When the Prophet would enter the toilet 'He said: ""O Allah! Indeed I seek refuge in You from Al-Khubith and Al- Khaba'ith."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 6)"
"1408","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: These privies are frequented by the jinns and devils. So when anyone amongst you goes there, he should say: ""I seek refuge in Allah from male and female devils."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 6)"
"1409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had not yet put it down from his blessed hand when the revelation was completed. He said: Allah Almighty has granted you women this concession; you may go out of your houses to relieve yourselves."
"1410","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(When performing istinja) whoever uses stones should use them in odd numbers; if he does so, it is good. And whoever goes to relieve himself should cover himself; if he finds nothing but a mound of sand to cover himself, then he should use that, because Satan plays with the private parts of the children of Adam.”"
"1411","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love what provided shelter or the fronds of palm trees."""""
"1412","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted his mule and seated me behind him. Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to relieve himself, he liked to do so behind a mound or behind a cluster of date palms. The narrator states: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to the garden of an Ansari."
"1413","When entering the Khala', the Messenger of Allah [SAW] would take off his ring. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5213)"
"1414","""The inscription on the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was in three lines: 'Muhammad' on a line, 'Messenger' on a line, and 'Allah' on a line."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1747)"
"1415","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Be on your guard against two things which provoke cursing. They (the companions present there) said: Messenger of Allah, what are those things which provoke cursing? He said: Easing on the thoroughfares or under the shades (where they take shelter and rest). (Using translation from Muslim 269)"
"1416","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""When any person goes to relieve himself, he should neither face the Qiblah nor turn his back towards it while defecating or urinating, but (from the perspective of Madinah) he should face towards the east or the west.\"" Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When we came to Syria, we found toilets built facing the direction of the Qiblah, so we wou"
"1417","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""When urinating or defecating, do not face towards the Qiblah nor turn your back towards it, but (according to the direction in Madinah) face towards the east or the west.\"" Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) states: When we came to Syria, there were toilets built facing the Qiblah. The narrator named Nu'man has transmitted these words: the"
"1418","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Once I climbed onto the roof of the house of Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her), and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was present there. He was relieving himself in the toilet facing the Qiblah and with his back towards Shaam."""""
"1419","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Harith Zubaidi on a Friday. He called for a basin and said to his maid, ""Make a curtain for"
"1420","I saw him urinating while facing the Qiblah."
"1421","I climbed onto the roof of my house and I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) relieving himself facing Bayt al-Maqdis."
"1422","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Two men should not sit together to relieve themselves in such a way that they are talking to each other and one of them is looking at the private parts of the other, because Allah Almighty is displeased with this."
"1423","I fear that Ibn Jurayj did not hear this narration from Nafi'."
"1424","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a garbage heap, he stood and urinated, then he performed ablution and wiped ove"
"1425","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) come to a garbage heap. He stood and urinated there, then he asked for water and performed ablution, wiping over his leather socks. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this action, there was no specific reason. It was not possible that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to a garbage heap, which was filthy. He intended to urinate there, but (to sit"
"1426","Ibn Hibban 1426 — Relieving oneself: Narration confirming the meaning of ""do not urinat..."
"1427","I came close to him until I stood behind him. I poured water for him, so he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"1428","""I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he came to some people's garbage dump and urinated while standing up. I turned to go away, but he called me back (to conceal him), and I was just behind him. Then when he had finished, he performed Wudu' and wiped over his Khuffs."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 18)"
"1429","Abu Musa inflicted extreme rigour upon himself in the matter of urination and urinated in a bottle and said: When the skin of anyone amongst the people of Israel was besmeared with urine, he cut that portion with a cutter. Hudhaifa said: I wish that'your friend should not inflict such an extreme rigour. I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were going together till we reached the dumping ground of filth behind an enclosure. He stood up as one among you would stand up. and he urinated, I tried to turn away from him, but he beckoned to me, so I went to him and I stood behind him, till he had relieved himself. (Using translation from Muslim 273b)"
"1430","Sayyiduna Hudhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him), which we have mentioned earlier. However, this is not the case, because Sayyiduna Hudhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him) saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) urinating by a wall near a heap of garbage, and this was at the outskirts of Madinah Munawwarah, and we have already explained the reason for this action of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was not with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at that time. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) urinating while sitting at home, so she narrated what she had seen, but Sayyiduna Hudhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated what he had seen. Therefore, Lady Aisha’s (may Allah be pleased with her) statement, ""declare him a liar,"" means that you should consider him mistaken, because sometimes the Arabs use the word ""lie"" (kathib) to mean ""mistake."
"1431","The Apostle of Allaah ( sal Allaahu alayhi wa sallam ) as saying: I am like father to you. When any of you goes to privy, he should not face or turn his back towards the qiblah. He should not cleanse with his right hand. He (the Prophet, sal Allaahu alayhi wa sallam) also commanded the Muslims to use three stones and forbade them to use dung or decayed bone. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 8)"
"1432","I asked 'Alqama if Ibn Mas'ud was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Jinn (the night when the Prophet met them). He (Ibn Mas'uad) said: No, but we were in the company of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night and we missed him. We searched for him in the valleys and the hills and said. He has either been taken away (by jinn) or has been secretly killed. He (the narrator) said. We spent the worst night which people could ever spend. When it was dawn we saw him coming from the side of Hiri'. He (the narrator) reported. We said: Messenger of Allah, we missed you and searched for you, but we could not find you and we spent the worst night which people could ever spend. He (the Holy Prophet) said: There came to me an inviter on behalf of the Jinn and I went along with him and recited to them the Qur'an. He (the narrator) said: He then went along with us and showed us their traces and traces of their embers. They (the Jinn) asked him (the Holy Prophet) about their provision and he said: Every bone on which the name of Allah is recited is your provision. The time it will fall in your hand it would be covered with flesh, and the dung of (the camels) is fodder for your animals. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Don't perform istinja with these (things) for these are the food of your brothers (Jinn). (Using translation from Muslim 450a)"
"1433","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man should touch his private part with his right hand."
"1434",": "" "" . Abdullah bin Abu Qatadah reports: My father told me this. He heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""When any person urinates, he should not touch his private part with his right hand, nor should he clean himself with his right hand."
"1435","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade cleaning oneself after relieving oneself with the right hand."
"1436","The Messenger of Allah said to me: 'When you perform ablution, clean your nose, and when you use pebbles to clean yourself after defecating, use an odd number.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 406)"
"1437","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""When a person uses stones, he should do so in an odd number, because Allah Almighty is Odd and He loves the odd. Have you not seen? The heavens are seven, the days are seven, the circuits of Tawaf are seven.\"" Then the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, mentioned some other things as well."""""
"1438","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this statement o"
"1439","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""When a person performs ablution, he should rinse his nose with water and clean it, and whoever uses stones (for cleaning), he should do so in an odd number."
"1440","The Apostle of Allaah ( sal Allaahu alayhi wa sallam ) as saying: I am like father to you. When any of you goes to privy, he should not face or turn his back towards the qiblah. He should not cleanse with his right hand. He (the Prophet, sal Allaahu alayhi wa sallam) also commanded the Muslims to use three stones and forbade them to use dung or decayed bone. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 8)"
"1441","I never saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) fasting during the (first) ten days of Dhul-Hijjah. Whenever he would return after relieving himself, he would use water."
"1442","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came out after relieving himself, I and a boy from the Ansar would bring a vessel of water, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform istinja (cleaning) with it."""""
"1443","Ibn Hibban 1443 — Relieving oneself: Clarifying that ""touching water"" in Aisha's narrat..."
"1444","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and I heard her saying that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would come out of the toilet, he used to say: ""Ghufranak"" (meaning: I seek Your forgiveness)."
"1445","I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt, Sayyida Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her). I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) get up, he relieved himself, then he washed his face and then went back to sleep."
"1446","A man said to him: ""Why don't you go out and fight?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Islam is built on five (pillars): Testimony that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, establishing Salah, giving Zakah, Hajj, and fasting Ramadan.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5001)"
"1447","""A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah enjoined upon His slaves?' He said: 'Allah has enjoined upon His slaves (five) prayers.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there anything before them or after them?' He said: 'Allah has enjoined upon His salves (five) prayers.' The man swore that he would not do anything more or less than that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If he is speaking the truth he will most certainly enter Paradise.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 459)"
"1448","Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) descended. He performed the prayer in front of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). So Umar bin Abdul Aziz said: O Urwah! Be mindful of what you are saying. So Urwah said: I heard Basheer bin Abu Mas’ood narrate this. I heard Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ood (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this, he says: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Jibreel (peace be upon him) descended, he performed the prayer, I prayed followi"
"1449","Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) informed Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about the timings of the prayers. Umar bin Abdul Aziz said to him: Consider carefully what you are saying. So Urwah said: I heard Basheer bin Abu Mas’ood narrate this, he says: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ood Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this, he says: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Jibreel descended and informed me about the time of the prayer, so I prayed with"
"1450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was commanded regarding this matter. So Umar bin Abdul Aziz said: O Urwah! Consider carefully what you are narrating. Would Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) establish the time of prayer for the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)? So Urwah said: Basheer bin Abu Mas’ud narrated the hadith from his father in the same way. Urwah narrates: Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) informed me that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the Asr prayer while the sunlight was still in the room of Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and it had not yet risen high."
"1451","that he said to ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar: ""Indeed, we find the prayer of the resident and the prayer of fear in the Quran, but we do not find the prayer of travel in the Quran?"" So ʿAbdullāh said to him: ""O son of my brother, indeed Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ to us and we do not know anything, so we only do as we have seen him do."""""
"1452","""We were with Sa'eed bin Al-'Asi in Tabaristan, and Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman was with us. He said: 'Which of you offered the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' Hudhaifah said: 'I did.' So Hudhaifah stood and the people formed two rows behind him, one row behind him and one row facing the enemy. He led those who were behind him in praying one rak'ah, then they went and took the place of the others, and the others came and he led them in praying one rak'ah, and they did not make it up."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1530)"
"1453","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is nothing between a person and disbelief except abandoning Salah.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 464)"
"1454","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The covenant that distinguishes between us and them is prayer; so whoever leaves it, he has committed Kufr.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1079)"
"1455","The time for prayer has come, but he remained silent. He delayed this prayer until after the twilight had disappeared and a part of the night had passed, then he dismounted and performed Maghrib and Isha prayers together. Then he explained that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to do the same when he wished to travel quickly."
"1456","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to combine two prayers on a journey, he delayed the noon prayer till came the early time of the afternoon prayer, and then combined the two. (Using translation from Muslim 704b)"
"1457","I forgive is that of the son of Rabi'ah bin Harith, who was a suckling child in the tribe of Hudhayl and was killed by them. Fear Allah regarding women, for you have taken them in Allah's trust, and their private parts have been made lawful to you by the word of Allah. You have a right over them that they do not allow anyone you dislike to come upon your bedding; if they do so, then you may strike them without severity. And they have a right over you that you provide for them with food and clothing in a fitting manner. I am leaving among you something that if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray after it: the Book of Allah. When you are asked about me, what will you say?"" The people said: ""We bear witness that you have conveyed (the message), fulfilled (the duty of Prophethood), and given good counsel."" Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) raised his forefinger towards the sky and then pointed it towards the people and said: ""O Allah! Bear witness."" He said this three times. Then the call to prayer was given, the Iqamah was said, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) led the Zuhr prayer. Then the Iqamah was said, and he led the Asr prayer. He did not perform any (supererogatory) prayer between the two. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) When it is permissible to perform the Asr prayer before its specific time and the one who does so does not deserve to be declared a disbeliever, then the one who delays the prayer and performs it after its time has passed is even more deserving not to be declared a disbeliever."
"1458","The Prophet ﷺ was engaged in the Battle of Tabuk. If he moved off before the sun had declined, he would delay the noon prayer till he would combine it with the afternoon prayer and would offer them together. If he moved off after the sun had declined, he would combine the noon and afternoon prayers, and then he proceeded; if he moved off before the evening prayer, he would delay the evening prayer; he would offer it along with the night prayer, he would delay the evening prayer; he would offer it along with the night prayer. If he moved off after the evening prayer, he would offer the night prayer earlier and offer it along with the evening prayer. Abu Dawud said: This tradition has not been narrated by anyone except by Qutaibah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1220)"
"1459","The time that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) set for the prayer, and his delaying the prayer until he left that valley, is a correct proof that a person who delays the prayer so much that its time passes does not become a disbeliever. Because if it were so, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would have instructed them to offer the prayer at the time when they woke up from sleep, and he would not have instructed them to move away from the place where they had slept, and the obligation for them would have been at the time when its time was still valid for them."
"1460","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no negligence when one sleeps, rather negligence is when one does not offer one prayer until the time of the next prayer comes and he realizes that he has missed a prayer.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 616)"
"1461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed the people, so they performed ablution. Then he ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and he gave the call to prayer (adhan). Then those people performed the two rak‘ahs of Fajr. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and he gave the iqamah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led the Fajr prayer. The people said: O Messenger of Allah! We have been negligent. Should we not repeat this prayer at its time tomorrow? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Your Lord forbids you from usury, so will He Himself accept it from you? Negligence occurs while awake."
"1462","The narrator states) The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not express displeasure towards either of the two groups. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) (If a person delays the prayer so much that the time for the next prayer begins, and if as a result of this, disbelief would necessarily apply to him, then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would not teach his Ummah something which, by doing so, would make them disbelievers. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would have expressed severe disapproval towards the person who committed this. His not expressing severe disapproval indicates that such a person does not become a disbeliever in a way that resembles apostasy.)"
"1463","narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On cloudy (i.e., overcast) days, perform the prayer early, for whoever abandons the prayer has committed disbelief. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Here, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has applied the term disbelief to the one who abandons the prayer because abandoning the prayer is the initial stage of disbelief. When a person abandons the prayer and makes it a habit, he sets out on the path of abandoning other obligations, and when he becomes accustomed to abandoning the obligations, this leads him towards denial. Thus, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has used the final name, which is the last part among the branches of disbelief, for the beginning, which is its first branch, and that is abandoning the prayer."
"1464","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Arguing about the Qur'an is disbelief."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) When a person starts arguing about the Qur'an, this leads him to such a state that, if Allah does not protect him, he becomes afflicted with doubts regarding the ambiguous verses, and when he becomes doubtful about a part of the Qur'an, this leads to denial. Therefore, the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, applied the term disbelief—which in reality is denial—at the very beginning of its cause, and that is arguing (about the Qur'an)."
"1465","narrated that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things are equivalent to disbelief in Allah: tearing the collar (of one's garment) while lamenting, wailing, and casting aspersions on someone's lineage."
